{
  "contract": "billing",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "description": "The decision corpus for standards/075-billing.md — the artifact that makes a polyglot entitlement standard enforceable from one source. An implementation loads 'catalog', 'subscriptions', 'ledger' and 'overrides' from the fixture, takes 'now' as the clock, then evaluates every case in 'checks' and either reproduces each expected result or names the case it failed. No running service, no provider and no network: the corpus is data and entitlementsFor(catalog, subscription, ledger, overrides, at) is a pure function of its arguments, which is what BL4 requires and why it requires it. A case's 'at' is the instant asked about; where absent it is 'now'. A case with 'before' is evaluated after the 'before' check, in the same process, against the same cache. The 'rejections' are stimuli an implementation must refuse or error on. Six cases are detectors, each written against a specific shortcut and checked against a reference implementation weakened that way. Four fail exactly one case: 'the-same-capability-inside-and-then-outside-the-grace-period' fails a cache of the current set keyed on tenant, catalog version and last ledger row without valid_until, once the clock moves; 'a-superseded-cancellation-never-takes-effect' fails a fold that applies rows in effective order rather than recorded order; 'the-last-day-of-a-cancelled-period-is-still-the-plan' fails an implementation that reads a pending cancellation as the status cancelled and suspends on it; 'an-override-that-expired-yesterday-contributes-nothing' fails an implementation that never reads expires_at. Two fail with company: 'the-plan-before-the-last-upgrade' fails an implementation that answers from the projection instead of the ledger, together with every other case asked about a date the projection does not describe; 'a-pending-downgrade-is-not-yet-applied' fails an implementation that applies every row at its recorded time, together with the cancelled-period case above and 'the-same-count-before-the-downgrade'. Each weakened implementation passes everything else.",
