      "expect": { "allowed": false, "reason": { "source": "plan", "id": "starter" } },
      "note": "DETECTOR. The tenant upgraded from starter to team on 10 August; asked about 1 August, the answer is starter's. An implementation that answers from the projection rather than folding the ledger to 'at' returns team and fails here while passing every current-time case (BL2, BL4)"
    },
    {
      "id": "a-quota-from-the-plan",
      "operation": "quotaFor",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_acme00000001", "metric": "seats" },
      "expect": { "value": 10, "source": { "source": "plan", "id": "team" } },
      "note": "the ceiling and where it came from"
    },
    {
      "id": "a-setting-read-as-configuration",
      "operation": "settingFor",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_acme00000001", "setting": "history_days" },
      "expect": { "value": 90, "source": { "source": "plan", "id": "team" } },
      "note": "a setting is read, never checked; it still says which plan fixed it (BL3)"
    },
    {
      "id": "an-allowance-mid-period",
      "operation": "allowanceFor",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_acme00000001", "metric": "api_calls" },
      "expect": {
        "value": 10000,
        "period_start": "2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z",
        "period_end": "2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z",
        "source": { "source": "plan", "id": "team" }
      },
      "note": "the ceiling and the period it resets on, taken from the subscription's current period; the usage itself is the domain's record and is not here (BL3)"
    },
    {
      "id": "an-allowance-fully-consumed",
      "operation": "withinAllowance",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_acme00000001", "metric": "api_calls", "used": 10000 },
      "expect": { "allowed": false, "reason": { "source": "plan", "id": "team" } },
      "note": "the domain passed its usage record; ten thousand used against a ceiling of ten thousand leaves nothing. The check keeps no counter of its own (BL4)"
    },
    {
      "id": "an-allowance-with-one-call-left",
      "operation": "withinAllowance",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_acme00000001", "metric": "api_calls", "used": 9999 },
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "reason": { "source": "plan", "id": "team" } },
      "note": "the boundary from the other side"
    },
    {
      "id": "past-due-one-day-inside-the-grace-period",
      "operation": "entitled",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_globex000001", "capability": "sso" },
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "reason": { "source": "plan", "id": "business" } },
      "note": "payment failed on 26 August at noon; the catalog's grace is fourteen days, so the plan contributes in full until 9 September at noon. Asked on 8 September at noon, the tenant has a day left (BL4)"
    },
    {
      "id": "the-same-capability-inside-and-then-outside-the-grace-period",
      "operation": "entitled",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_globex000001", "capability": "sso", "at": "2026-09-10T12:00:00.000Z" },
      "expect": { "allowed": false, "reason": { "source": "suspended", "id": "past_due" } },
      "before": {
        "operation": "entitled",
        "check": { "tenant": "ten_globex000001", "capability": "sso" },
        "expect": { "allowed": true }
      },
      "note": "DETECTOR, and THE CACHE CASE. Evaluate 'before' at now, then this check one day past the grace period, with no ledger row between the two. A cache keyed on tenant, catalog version and last ledger row alone sees nothing change and returns allowed twice; a cache that honours the set's valid_until — the grace end, 9 September at noon — does not. This is why the entitlement cache carries a time boundary that a permission cache never needed (BL4)"
    },
    {
      "id": "a-suspended-quota-is-zero",
      "operation": "quotaFor",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_globex000001", "metric": "seats", "at": "2026-09-10T12:00:00.000Z" },
      "expect": { "value": 0, "source": { "source": "suspended", "id": "past_due" } },
      "note": "the suspended set: every quota and allowance is zero, so nothing new is created, and the source says why (BL4)"
    },
    {
      "id": "a-setting-survives-suspension",
      "operation": "settingFor",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_globex000001", "setting": "history_days", "at": "2026-09-10T12:00:00.000Z" },
      "expect": { "value": 365, "source": { "source": "plan", "id": "business" } },
      "note": "a setting keeps the plan's value while suspended, because how long history is kept is exactly what governs a tenant that has stopped paying (BL4)"
    },
    {
      "id": "the-derived-set-with-its-next-boundary",
      "operation": "entitlementsFor",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_globex000001" },
      "expect": {
        "tenant_id": "ten_globex000001",
        "at": "2026-09-08T12:00:00.000Z",
        "plan": "business",
        "status": "past_due",
        "suspended": false,
        "catalog_version": "2026-09",
        "capabilities": ["audit_export", "custom_domains", "sso"],
        "quotas": {
          "projects": { "value": null, "source": { "source": "plan", "id": "business" } },
          "seats": { "value": 50, "source": { "source": "plan", "id": "business" } }
        },
        "allowances": {
          "api_calls": {
            "value": 100000,
            "period_start": "2026-08-15T00:00:00.000Z",
            "period_end": "2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z",
            "source": { "source": "plan", "id": "business" }
          }
        },
        "settings": {
          "history_days": { "value": 365, "source": { "source": "plan", "id": "business" } }
        },
        "pending_change": null,
        "trial_end": null,
        "valid_until": "2026-09-09T12:00:00.000Z"
      },
      "note": "the whole set, as /me carries it (060 AU6): capabilities sorted and complete, every value with its source, and valid_until naming the grace end rather than the later period end, because it is the earliest instant the set would differ with no new row. catalog_version is the catalog the set was derived from, not the version the tenant is priced under: entitlements are current, prices are grandfathered (BL1, BL4)"
    },
    {
      "id": "no-ceiling-is-not-zero",
      "operation": "withinQuota",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_globex000001", "metric": "projects", "current": 100000 },
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "reason": { "source": "plan", "id": "business" } },
      "note": "business has no ceiling on projects; null means unlimited, and an implementation that treats it as zero refuses everything (BL3)"
    },
    {
      "id": "the-last-day-of-a-cancelled-period-is-still-the-plan",
      "operation": "entitled",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_initech00001", "capability": "audit_export" },
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "reason": { "source": "plan", "id": "team" } },
      "note": "DETECTOR. The tenant cancelled on 20 August; the row takes effect at period end, 9 September at midnight. On 8 September the plan still contributes in full: the tenant keeps what it paid for. An implementation that applies the suspended set from the recorded time refuses here and passes every other case (BL2, BL7)"
    },
    {
      "id": "the-first-day-after-a-cancelled-period",
      "operation": "entitled",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_initech00001", "capability": "audit_export", "at": "2026-09-09T12:00:00.000Z" },
      "expect": { "allowed": false, "reason": { "source": "suspended", "id": "cancelled" } },
      "note": "twelve hours after the row took effect: no plan, the suspended set, and the reason names the status that caused it (BL4)"
    },
    {
      "id": "a-pending-downgrade-is-not-yet-applied",
      "operation": "entitled",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_umbrella0001", "capability": "sso" },
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "reason": { "source": "plan", "id": "business" } },
      "note": "DETECTOR. A downgrade to team was recorded on 2 September, effective 20 September. Until then it is the pending change and business contributes in full. An implementation that applies a downgrade at recording refuses here (BL2, BL7)"
    },
    {
      "id": "a-pending-downgrade-once-applied",
      "operation": "entitled",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_umbrella0001", "capability": "sso", "at": "2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z" },
      "expect": { "allowed": false, "reason": { "source": "plan", "id": "team" } },
      "note": "the day after the row took effect, the same question has team's answer"
    },
    {
      "id": "a-quota-already-exceeded-after-a-downgrade",
      "operation": "withinQuota",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_umbrella0001", "metric": "seats", "current": 27, "at": "2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z" },
      "expect": { "allowed": false, "reason": { "source": "plan", "id": "team" } },
      "note": "twenty-seven seats exist and team allows ten. Nothing is deleted and nothing new is created: the twenty-eighth is refused until the count is under the ceiling (BL7)"
    },
    {
      "id": "the-same-count-before-the-downgrade",
      "operation": "withinQuota",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_umbrella0001", "metric": "seats", "current": 27 },
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "reason": { "source": "plan", "id": "business" } },
      "note": "the same domain count against the plan still in force: business allows fifty"
    },
    {
      "id": "an-override-that-expired-yesterday-contributes-nothing",
      "operation": "quotaFor",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_hooli0000001", "metric": "seats" },
      "expect": { "value": 3, "source": { "source": "plan", "id": "starter" } },
      "note": "DETECTOR. The seats override of eight expired on 7 September at noon; asked on 8 September at noon, the plan's three is the answer. An implementation that never reads expires_at returns eight and passes every other case (BL4)"
    },
    {
      "id": "the-same-override-the-day-before-it-expired",
      "operation": "quotaFor",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_hooli0000001", "metric": "seats", "at": "2026-09-06T12:00:00.000Z" },
      "expect": { "value": 8, "source": { "source": "override", "id": "ovr_000000000001" } },
      "note": "the override wins over the plan while it lives, and the source names it rather than the plan (BL4)"
    },
    {
      "id": "a-capability-granted-by-a-live-override",
      "operation": "entitled",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_hooli0000001", "capability": "audit_export" },
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "reason": { "source": "override", "id": "ovr_000000000002" } },
      "note": "starter does not carry audit_export; an administrator granted it until November with a reason, and the reason on the row is what an administrator reads on a support call (BL2, BL4)"
    },
    {
      "id": "a-trial-contributes-the-full-plan",
      "operation": "entitled",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_vandelay0001", "capability": "audit_export" },
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "reason": { "source": "plan", "id": "team" } },
      "note": "trialing is the full plan; a trial that shows less than the plan is a demonstration of something else (BL8)"
    },
    {
      "id": "a-quota-at-its-ceiling-refuses-one-more",
      "operation": "withinQuota",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_vandelay0001", "metric": "projects", "current": 25 },
      "expect": { "allowed": false, "reason": { "source": "plan", "id": "team" } },
      "note": "twenty-five exist and team allows twenty-five; the question is whether one more fits, and it does not (BL3)"
    },
    {
      "id": "a-superseded-cancellation-never-takes-effect",
      "operation": "entitled",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_wayne0000001", "capability": "audit_export" },
      "expect": { "allowed": true, "reason": { "source": "plan", "id": "team" } },
      "note": "DETECTOR. A cancellation recorded on 5 August, effective 1 September, was superseded by a reactivation recorded on 20 August. Rows are applied in recorded order and a row recorded while another is pending supersedes it, so on 8 September the tenant is active on team. An implementation that sorts by effective time applies the reactivation and then the cancellation, and refuses here while passing every other case (BL2)"
    },
    {
      "id": "an-expired-trial-is-suspended",
      "operation": "entitled",
      "check": { "tenant": "ten_stark0000001", "capability": "audit_export" },
      "expect": { "allowed": false, "reason": { "source": "suspended", "id": "cancelled" } },
      "note": "the trial.expire job wrote trial_expired with actor job; an expired trial is a cancellation that never paid, and the suspended set applies from that instant (BL8)"
    }
  ],
  "rejections": [
    {
      "id": "catalog-with-a-dotted-capability-id-is-refused",
      "stimulus": "validate a catalog whose capabilities include the id 'audit.export'",
      "expect": { "refused": true },
      "note": "a capability never has a dot; a permission always has exactly one. The schema refuses it so that no identifier can be mistaken for the wrong kind (BL3)"
    },
    {
      "id": "ledger-row-with-an-unknown-kind-is-refused",
      "stimulus": "insert a ledger row of kind 'renewed'",
      "expect": { "refused": true },
      "note": "the kind set is closed; a renewal changes neither plan nor status and updates the projection's period fields without a row. A transition outside the set is a schema failure, not a new row (BL2)"
    },
    {
      "id": "subscription-with-two-pending-changes-is-refused",
      "stimulus": "store a projection carrying two pending changes, or record a second future-effective row for a tenant without it superseding the first",
      "expect": { "refused": true },
      "note": "pending_change is one object or null, never an array, and a row recorded while another is pending supersedes it. Two scheduled changes have no defined order and the projection cannot show both (BL2)"
    },
    {
      "id": "per-user-entitlement-is-refused",
      "stimulus": "store an override or a subscription carrying a user_id, declare a capability whose subject is a user, or call entitled() with a user rather than a tenant",
      "expect": { "refused": true },
      "note": "nothing is per user. What one person may do inside a tenant is a permission under 070; a per-seat price is a quota on seats. The schemas have no field for it and the operations take no user (BL3)"
    },
    {
      "id": "plan-missing-a-declared-metric-is-refused",
      "stimulus": "validate a catalog that declares the quota metric 'projects' and a plan whose quotas omit it",
      "expect": { "refused": true },
      "note": "every plan gives a value for every declared metric and setting; an absent ceiling is neither zero nor unlimited and the function would have to guess. A cross-reference the schema cannot express, so the corpus holds it (BL1)"
    },
    {
      "id": "plan-listing-an-undeclared-capability-is-refused",
      "stimulus": "validate a catalog in which a plan's capabilities include 'white_glove' and no capability of that id is declared",
      "expect": { "refused": true },
      "note": "a plan composes capabilities the catalog declares, the way a role composes permissions the code declares (070 RB3). A capability that appears only in a plan has no check behind it and grants nothing silently (BL1, BL3)"
    },
    {
      "id": "float-price-is-refused",
      "stimulus": "validate a catalog in which a price's amount is 19.99",
      "expect": { "refused": true },
      "note": "money is integer minor units plus an explicit currency (020 IP5); the schema refers to that def and admits nothing else (BL1)"
    },
    {
      "id": "check-against-an-undeclared-capability-errors",
      "stimulus": "call entitled() with 'audit_exprot'",
      "expect": { "error": true },
      "note": "an error, not a denial. A denial is indistinguishable from a correct refusal and hides the typo forever (BL4, the same reasoning as 070 RB1)"
    },
    {
      "id": "ledger-row-update-or-delete-is-refused",
      "stimulus": "issue UPDATE or DELETE against a ledger row under the service's own credential",
      "expect": { "refused": true },
      "note": "append-only means the writes are the only writes: INSERT and SELECT, and no code path that alters a row. A correction is a new row with a reason (BL2, 080 AE6's discipline)"
    },
    {
      "id": "duplicate-provider-event-is-refused",
      "stimulus": "record a second ledger row carrying a provider_event_id already recorded for the tenant",
      "expect": { "refused": true },
      "note": "a redelivered webhook is a repeat under 055 AM3 and never a second transition; the provider's event id on the row is what makes the constraint checkable without provider-specific logic (BL6)"
    }
  ]
}
